concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018-sch-1-sec-76 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "76 Subsection 180B(3)"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-76 ;
    values:originalText "Repeal the subsection, substitute:  (3) The authorised officer must not make the authorisation unless:  (a) the Attorney-General has authorised the making of the authorisation under a provision mentioned in an item of the following table; and  (b) the authorised officer is satisfied that:  (i) the disclosure is reasonably necessary for an investigation or proceeding referred to in that table item; and  (ii) the disclosure is appropriate in all the circumstances.  Authorising access to prospective information or documents Item For Attorney-General authorisations under: the investigation or proceeding is: section 15D of the Mutual an investigation or proceeding relating  Assistance to international courts and tribunals  Schedule 1 Prospective telecommunications data  Part 5  No. 34, 2018 Crimes Legislation Amendment (International Crime Cooperation and Other Measures) Act 2018  Authorising access to prospective information or documents Item For Attorney-General authorisations under: the investigation or proceeding is: Assistance in Criminal Matters Act 1987 to an offence against the law of a foreign country that: (a) is punishable by imprisonment for 3 years or more, imprisonment for life or the death penalty; or (b) involves an act or omission that, if it had occurred in Australia, would be a serious offence section 78B of the International Criminal Court Act 2002 an investigation or proceeding relating to a crime within the jurisdiction of the ICC section 34B of the International War Crimes Tribunals Act 1995 an investigation or proceeding relating to a War Crimes Tribunal offence" ;
    skos:definition "Repeal the subsection, substitute:  (3) The authorised officer must not make the authorisation unless:  (a) the Attorney-General has authorised the making of the authorisation under a provision mentioned in an item of the following table; and  (b) the authorised officer is satisfied that:  (i) the disclosure is reasonably necessary for an investigation or proceeding referred to in that table item; and  (ii) the disclosure is appropriate in all the circumstances.  Authorising access to prospective information or documents Item For Attorney-General authorisations under: the investigation or proceeding is: section 15D of the Mutual an investigation or proceeding relating  Assistance to international courts and tribunals  Schedule 1 Prospective telecommunications data  Part 5  No. 34, 2018 Crimes Legislation Amendment (International Crime Cooperation and Other Measures) Act 2018  Authorising access to prospective information or documents Item For Attorney-General authorisations under: the investigation or proceeding is: Assistance in Criminal Matters Act 1987 to an offence against the law of a foreign country that: (a) is punishable by imprisonment for 3 years or more, imprisonment for life or the death penalty; or (b) involves an act or omission that, if it had occurred in Australia, would be a serious offence section 78B of the International Criminal Court Act 2002 an investigation or proceeding relating to a crime within the jurisdiction of the ICC section 34B of the International War Crimes Tribunals Act 1995 an investigation or proceeding relating to a War Crimes Tribunal offence"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "9d704bceeaabb42633f0f921f704c0ce4cd95b28f5aa09e798628d1fe9f394cd" ;
    cof:pageNumber "34"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Authorisation must be made under specific conditions." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018.pdf> ;
    dc:source "crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018.pdf, p.34" ;
    cml:asserts concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018-sch-1-sec-76-norm .
