concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018-sch-1-sec-79a a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "79A Authorising applications for surveillance device warrants"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-79a ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Attorney-General may authorise, in writing, an eligible law enforcement officer to apply for a surveillance device warrant under section 14 of the Surveillance Devices Act 2004 if:  (a) the ICC has requested the Attorney-General to arrange for the use of a surveillance device; and  (b) the Attorney-General is satisfied that an investigation is being conducted by the Prosecutor, or a proceeding is before the ICC; and  (c) the Attorney-General is satisfied that the ICC has given appropriate undertakings for:  (i) ensuring that the information obtained as a result of the use of the device will only be used for the purpose for which it is communicated to the ICC; and  (ii) the destruction of a document or other thing containing information obtained as a result of the use of the device; and  (iii) any other matter the Attorney-General considers appropriate. Note: The eligible law enforcement officer can only apply for the warrant if he or she reasonably suspects that the use of the device is necessary  Schedule 1  Assistance to international courts and tribunals" ;
    skos:definition "(1) The Attorney-General may authorise, in writing, an eligible law enforcement officer to apply for a surveillance device warrant under section 14 of the Surveillance Devices Act 2004 if:  (a) the ICC has requested the Attorney-General to arrange for the use of a surveillance device; and  (b) the Attorney-General is satisfied that an investigation is being conducted by the Prosecutor, or a proceeding is before the ICC; and  (c) the Attorney-General is satisfied that the ICC has given appropriate undertakings for:  (i) ensuring that the information obtained as a result of the use of the device will only be used for the purpose for which it is communicated to the ICC; and  (ii) the destruction of a document or other thing containing information obtained as a result of the use of the device; and  (iii) any other matter the Attorney-General considers appropriate. Note: The eligible law enforcement officer can only apply for the warrant if he or she reasonably suspects that the use of the device is necessary  Schedule 1  Assistance to international courts and tribunals"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "b8e9ff4d914552545b626650d7026a03bc41c08d99d90c86f463719d0c4a1068" ;
    cof:pageNumber "37"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "The Attorney-General may authorise an eligible law enforcement officer to apply for a surveillance device warrant." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018.pdf> ;
    dc:source "crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018.pdf, p.37" ;
    cml:asserts concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018-sch-1-sec-79a-norm .
