concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018-sch-1-sec-76a a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "76A Authorising application for carrying out of forensic procedures"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-76a ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Attorney-General may authorise, in writing, a constable to apply under Part ID of the Crimes Act 1914 for an order for the carrying out of a forensic procedure on a person if:  (a) the ICC has requested the procedure to be carried out on the person; and  (b) the Attorney-General is satisfied:  (i) that the request relates to an investigation being conducted by the Prosecutor or a proceeding before the ICC; and  (ii) that the person is, or is believed to be, in Australia; and  Schedule 1  Assistance to international courts and tribunals" ;
    skos:definition "(1) The Attorney-General may authorise, in writing, a constable to apply under Part ID of the Crimes Act 1914 for an order for the carrying out of a forensic procedure on a person if:  (a) the ICC has requested the procedure to be carried out on the person; and  (b) the Attorney-General is satisfied:  (i) that the request relates to an investigation being conducted by the Prosecutor or a proceeding before the ICC; and  (ii) that the person is, or is believed to be, in Australia; and  Schedule 1  Assistance to international courts and tribunals"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "4e0f722a341a77e39adc63b30ac805ba6680f1ddfd12737324d78cf1288bf872" ;
    cof:pageNumber "53"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Authorisation for carrying out forensic procedures" ;
