concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018-sch-1-sec-76b a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "76B Providing forensic evidence to the ICC"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-76b ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Attorney-General may direct a constable about how forensic evidence is to be provided to the ICC if:  (a) the Attorney-General gave an authorisation to the constable under subsection 76A(1); and  (b) the forensic evidence resulted from the authorisation.  Assistance to international courts and tribunals  Schedule 1 Forensic procedures  Part 7  No. 34, 2018 Crimes Legislation Amendment (International Crime Cooperation and Other Measures) Act 2018  (2) A direction under subsection (1) is not a legislative instrument. International War Crimes Tribunals Act 1995" ;
    skos:definition "(1) The Attorney-General may direct a constable about how forensic evidence is to be provided to the ICC if:  (a) the Attorney-General gave an authorisation to the constable under subsection 76A(1); and  (b) the forensic evidence resulted from the authorisation.  Assistance to international courts and tribunals  Schedule 1 Forensic procedures  Part 7  No. 34, 2018 Crimes Legislation Amendment (International Crime Cooperation and Other Measures) Act 2018  (2) A direction under subsection (1) is not a legislative instrument. International War Crimes Tribunals Act 1995"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "fe7581d6245cb487a904f653486303f6dcbc6c1a655bbb9b75d390de7d3017a4" ;
    cof:pageNumber "54"^^xsd:integer ;
