concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018-sch-1-sec-32c a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "32C Providing forensic evidence to the Tribunal"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-32c ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Attorney-General may direct a constable about how forensic evidence is to be provided to a Tribunal if:  (a) the Attorney-General gave an authorisation to the constable under subsection 32B(1); and  (b) the forensic evidence resulted from the authorisation.  Assistance to international courts and tribunals  Schedule 1 Forensic procedures  Part 7  No. 34, 2018 Crimes Legislation Amendment (International Crime Cooperation and Other Measures) Act 2018  (2) A direction under subsection (1) is not a legislative instrument." ;
    skos:definition "(1) The Attorney-General may direct a constable about how forensic evidence is to be provided to a Tribunal if:  (a) the Attorney-General gave an authorisation to the constable under subsection 32B(1); and  (b) the forensic evidence resulted from the authorisation.  Assistance to international courts and tribunals  Schedule 1 Forensic procedures  Part 7  No. 34, 2018 Crimes Legislation Amendment (International Crime Cooperation and Other Measures) Act 2018  (2) A direction under subsection (1) is not a legislative instrument."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "2c1ce45e5692b074e33320d18ffcac8443b317e8f19b3c97d0eabbbb1e619dcb" ;
    cof:pageNumber "56"^^xsd:integer ;
