concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018-sch-6-sec-26 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "26 At the end of section 270.10 of the Criminal Code"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-6-sec-26 ;
    values:originalText "Add:  (4) In this section: family member of a person means:  (a) the person’s spouse or de facto partner; or  (b) a parent, step-parent or grandparent of the person; or  Slavery-like offences and relevant evidence  Schedule 6 Relevant evidence  Part 2  No. 34, 2018 Crimes Legislation Amendment (International Crime Cooperation and Other Measures) Act 2018  (c) a child, step-child or grandchild of the person; or  (d) a brother, sister, step-brother or step-sister of the person; or  (e) a guardian or carer of the person.  (5) For the purposes of this section, the family members of a person are taken to include the following (without limitation):  (a) a de facto partner of the person;  (b) someone who is the child of the person, or of whom the person is the child, because of the definition of child in the Dictionary;  (c) anyone else who would be a member of the person’s family if someone mentioned in paragraph (a) or (b) is taken to be a family member of the person." ;
    skos:definition "Add:  (4) In this section: family member of a person means:  (a) the person’s spouse or de facto partner; or  (b) a parent, step-parent or grandparent of the person; or  Slavery-like offences and relevant evidence  Schedule 6 Relevant evidence  Part 2  No. 34, 2018 Crimes Legislation Amendment (International Crime Cooperation and Other Measures) Act 2018  (c) a child, step-child or grandchild of the person; or  (d) a brother, sister, step-brother or step-sister of the person; or  (e) a guardian or carer of the person.  (5) For the purposes of this section, the family members of a person are taken to include the following (without limitation):  (a) a de facto partner of the person;  (b) someone who is the child of the person, or of whom the person is the child, because of the definition of child in the Dictionary;  (c) anyone else who would be a member of the person’s family if someone mentioned in paragraph (a) or (b) is taken to be a family member of the person."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "f552a1e79bdc74d313b3f0f000e309faa363c9b81f8db6b9d0fb2b41f0dcea48" ;
    cof:pageNumber "110"^^xsd:integer ;
