doc:sch-6-sec-30 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "30 At the end of section 271.11A of the Criminal Code" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "Add:  (5) In this section: family member of a person means:  (a) the person’s spouse or de facto partner; or  (b) a parent, step-parent or grandparent of the person; or  (c) a child, step-child or grandchild of the person; or  (d) a brother, sister, step-brother or step-sister of the person; or  (e) a guardian or carer of the person.  Schedule 6  Slavery-like offences and relevant evidence" ;
    cof:pageNumber "111"^^xsd:integer .

concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018-sch-6-sec-31 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "31 Application of amendments"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-6-sec-31 ;
    values:originalText "(1) The amendments made by Part 1 of this Schedule apply in relation to conduct engaged in on or after the commencement of this item. (2) The amendments made by Part 2 of this Schedule apply in relation to proceedings for offences instituted after the commencement of this item (whether the proceedings are for offences committed, or alleged to have been committed, before or after the commencement of this item)." ;
    skos:definition "(1) The amendments made by Part 1 of this Schedule apply in relation to conduct engaged in on or after the commencement of this item. (2) The amendments made by Part 2 of this Schedule apply in relation to proceedings for offences instituted after the commencement of this item (whether the proceedings are for offences committed, or alleged to have been committed, before or after the commencement of this item)."@en ;
