doc:sch-11-sec-5a-ss-3 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "5A(3) Declaration of major national events" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(3) In considering whether to make a declaration under subsection (1) in relation to an event, the Minister may have regard to:  (a) the significance of the event; and  (b) the need (if any) to coordinate security arrangements in relation to the event with one or more States or Territories or one or more foreign governments; and  (c) any risk assessment relating to the event; and  (d) the potential impact of any security incident relating to the event on Australia’s reputation; and  (e) the anticipated attendees at the event; and  (f) any other matter the Minister considers relevant.  Schedule 11  Amendment of the AusCheck Act 2007  Crimes Legislation Amendment (International Crime Cooperation and Other Measures) Act 2018 No. 34, 2018" ;
    cof:pageNumber "125"^^xsd:integer .

concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018-sch-11-sec-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "3 At the end of subsection 8(1)"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-11-sec-3 ;
    values:originalText "Add:  ; or (d) the check is of an individual in connection with the accreditation of the individual in relation to a major national event." ;
    skos:definition "Add:  ; or (d) the check is of an individual in connection with the accreditation of the individual in relation to a major national event."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "187910e0b5a20214cfd0e985032f783180271a874a5e81b69df0b519de80747e" ;
