concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018-sch-11-sec-10aa a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "10AA Matters covered by the AusCheck scheme—background"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-11-sec-10aa ;
    values:originalText "checks in connection with major national events  (1) The AusCheck scheme may, for the purposes of paragraph 8(1)(d), make provision for and in relation to any of the following:  (a) the giving to the Secretary of information, relating to an individual in respect of whom a background check is conducted, that is directly necessary for the purpose of conducting the background check;  (b) the criteria against which a background check is to be assessed;  (c) the decision or decisions that may be made as a result of a background check;  (d) the form of advice to be given to an individual in respect of whom a background check is conducted;  Schedule 11  Amendment of the AusCheck Act 2007  Crimes Legislation Amendment (International Crime Cooperation and Other Measures) Act 2018 No. 34, 2018  (e) the form of advice to be given to other persons about the outcome of a background check.  (2) The matters referred to in subsection (1) may relate to:  (a) all background checks to be conducted for the purposes of paragraph 8(1)(d); or  (b) a specified class of background checks.  [Minister’s second reading speech made in— House of Representatives on 23 November 2016 Senate on 13 February 2018]  (178/16)" ;
    skos:definition "checks in connection with major national events  (1) The AusCheck scheme may, for the purposes of paragraph 8(1)(d), make provision for and in relation to any of the following:  (a) the giving to the Secretary of information, relating to an individual in respect of whom a background check is conducted, that is directly necessary for the purpose of conducting the background check;  (b) the criteria against which a background check is to be assessed;  (c) the decision or decisions that may be made as a result of a background check;  (d) the form of advice to be given to an individual in respect of whom a background check is conducted;  Schedule 11  Amendment of the AusCheck Act 2007  Crimes Legislation Amendment (International Crime Cooperation and Other Measures) Act 2018 No. 34, 2018  (e) the form of advice to be given to other persons about the outcome of a background check.  (2) The matters referred to in subsection (1) may relate to:  (a) all background checks to be conducted for the purposes of paragraph 8(1)(d); or  (b) a specified class of background checks.  [Minister’s second reading speech made in— House of Representatives on 23 November 2016 Senate on 13 February 2018]  (178/16)"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "bf5d7ebbb85e647036abba1905500d9ba05600441ce74a07635cc4ef03b6f672" ;
    cof:pageNumber "127"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018-sch-11-sec-10aa-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-international-crime-cooperation-and-other-measures-act-2018-sch-11-sec-10aa-ss-2 ;
